<title>LEBANON: Lebanese bank assets up 20% Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>Lebanese bank assets up 20% Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total assets of Lebanon's banks rose 19.69 percent in the first 10 months of the year, the Lebanese Banks Association reported.</p>
<p>The Association issued the following details (in billions of Lebanese pounds, at end of period unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>		    Dec 95   Aug 96   Sep 96   Oct 96   Dec95-Oct96</p>
<p> % Total Assets 29.055  32.892    33.353   34.775   19.69</p>
<p> Month change (%)	  1.26	1.40     4.26</p>
<p>Deposits of Residents and Non-residents</p>
<p>		  23,884    27,342    27,663   29,062   21.68</p>
<p> Month change (%)	  1.15	1.17     5.06</p>
<p>Claims on Residents and Non-residents</p>
<p>		  10,695    12,200    12,376   12,613   17.93</p>
<p> Month change (%)	  0.06	1.44     1.91</p>
<p> Total capital 1,146     1,389     1,385    1,401   22.26</p>
<p> Month change (%)	  1.71     (0.26)    1.17</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078 645456</p>
</text>
